# examples/discord_bot — environment template. cp .env.example .env, then edit.
#
# run_discord_bot.py loads this file at startup (run_discord_bot.py:488) and
# preflights the keys before connecting, naming whatever is missing.
#
# Uncomment and fill in what you need; leave the rest commented. An empty
# value ("OPENAI_API_KEY=") still registers the name in os.environ, and
# models/model_factory.py checks presence rather than truth, so a blank line
# hides the "key is required" error behind a 401 from the provider.

# --- Required for live mode ---
# DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=       Discord developer portal -> Reset Token. Shown once.

# --- Required: agent.yaml is provider: openai, model: gpt-5.4 ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Swap for GOOGLE_API_KEY (or GEMINI_API_KEY) if you repoint provider: google,
# or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for provider: anthropic.

# --- Required by the tavily_search tool in agent.yaml ---
# TAVILY_API_KEY=          or drop tavily_search from the tools list.

# --- Optional ---
# SDK_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG
